        <definition>void themis::scraper::BurstCrawlController::refill</definition>
        <argsstring>() noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>refill</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::scraper::BurstCrawlController::refill</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Top-up the bucket for time elapsed since the last refill. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Protected by <computeroutput>refill_mu_</computeroutput> to serialise the elapsed-time calculation and <computeroutput>last_refill_</computeroutput> update. The actual token store is still atomic so that <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_burst_crawl_controller_1aa76f79eaadd04810a02181dcaadf7be9" kindref="member">tryAcquire()</ref></computeroutput> CAS loops remain correct even if multiple threads race through this path. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="include/scraper/scraper_burst_controller.h" line="133" column="10" bodyfile="include/scraper/scraper_burst_controller.h" bodystart="133" bodyend="169"/>
      </memberdef>
    </sectiondef>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Fail-fast token-bucket rate limiter for URL dispatch. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Thread-safe: <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_burst_crawl_controller_1aa76f79eaadd04810a02181dcaadf7be9" kindref="member">tryAcquire()</ref></computeroutput> and <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_burst_crawl_controller_1abf99f988b305bf9547bf9f6346e8ea73" kindref="member">burstUtilization()</ref></computeroutput> may be called concurrently from multiple threads. <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1scraper_1_1_burst_crawl_controller_1ac47e175558835107e3f2e602543abf29" kindref="member">reset()</ref></computeroutput> serialises via the same refill mutex. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
